This all looks correct — the bottom-of-page edge case is handled, and the active-class toggling logic is right.

One small cleanup note: in header, you have padding-top: $section-padding; immediately followed by padding-top: 100px; — the second declaration silently overrides the first, so the $section-padding line is dead code right now. Just delete that first line so it's clear you intentionally want 100px there (or better, make a named variable like $nav-clearance: 100px so it's self-documenting):

header{
    padding-top: 100px;
    padding-bottom: $section-padding;
