Good time to test the whole indicator end-to-end once real content exists. Let's move to:

Step 8: Host Cities — multi-column layout

Concept: "3+ columns" is most simply done with CSS Grid — it's the modern, purpose-built tool for 2D layouts like this (rows and columns), and easier to reason about than floats or inline-blocks.

HTML — add city cards inside #host-cities .container:

<section id="host-cities">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Host Cities</h2>
        <div class="city-grid">
            <div class="city-card">
                <h3>Mexico City</h3>
